      "writtenOn": "2024-10-31T13:58:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This log looks very similar to the situation I observed locally while running the test with `stress -c $(nproc)` (described in detail here: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/5966976/comments/72e92f0b_52fb3d0f). I\u0027ve hacked together a small change that will save the UART log from Renode into an additional file and print the contents of this file if the test fails: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/5979545/1. If the `Pass!` string is not visible in this file that means that the test didn\u0027t finish successfully. If `Pass!` is visible that suggests that there was an error during communication between Renode and the `run_device_tests.py` script. It would be great if you could run the test with this patch and share the results, so we can better understand what is causing the timeouts.",
